        {
            "_id": "UEWE0iejBm2XsMuO",
            "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Passive.webp",
            "name": "Solstice Dependent",
            "sort": 1300000,
            "system": {
                "actionType": {
                    "value": "passive"
                },
                "actions": {
                    "value": null
                },
                "category": "defensive",
                "description": {
                    "value": "<p>A hora is mystically bonded to a natural location with a simple astronomical calendar that marks the summer and winter solstice. If they aren't at that location at dawn when the sunlight touches the calendar, they become @UUID[Compendium.pf2e.conditionitems.Item.Drained]{Drained 1}, increasing the value by 1 for each missed day and reducing by 1 only when they witness dawn's light touch the calendar. Even on a cloudy day, there's enough sunlight to satisfy the hora's need. A hora can perform a 24-hour ritual to bond to a new location.</p>"
                },
                "publication": {
                    "license": "OGL",
                    "remaster": false,
                    "title": ""
                },
                "rules": [],
                "slug": null,
                "traits": {
                    "value": []
                }
            },
            "type": "action"
        },
        {
            "_id": "24nEftgKJZX1ExCP",
            "img": "systems/pf2e/icons/actions/Reaction.webp",
            "name": "Summer's Rescue",
            "sort": 1400000,
            "system": {
                "actionType": {
                    "value": "reaction"
                },
                "actions": {
                    "value": null
                },
                "category": "offensive",
                "description": {
                    "value": "<p><strong>Trigger</strong> The summer hora or an ally within 30 feet that the summer hora can see fails a Perception check or saving throw</p><hr /><p><strong>Effect</strong> The hora's or ally's check gains a retroactive status bonus, which can change the outcome from a critical failure to a failure or a failure to a success. This bonus is +2 in summer, increasing to +4 if it's within 14 days of the summer solstice. In spring or autumn, the bonus is +1, and in winter this ability has no effect. The summer hora can't use Summer's Rescue again for [[/gmr 1d4 #Recharge Summer's Rescue]]{1d4 rounds}.</p>"
                },
                "publication": {
